Regional Outlook
North America: The region leads the market, supported by established nuclear infrastructure, radioactive-waste management programs, and investment in storage, treatment, and decommissioning services.
Asia-Pacific: Expansion of nuclear programs and investment in energy infrastructure create opportunities for waste-management providers, particularly in interim storage, treatment, and long-term disposal planning.

Why This Market Matters
Effective nuclear-waste management is essential to protecting public health, limiting environmental contamination, and supporting the long-term operation and decommissioning of nuclear facilities. It also influences the cost and public acceptance of nuclear energy projects. Market participants must address technical complexity, long project timelines, high capital requirements, and the need for sustained regulatory oversight.

